# Accessibility (UI)

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| Type | Rule |
| Audience | Developer and tester when the specification has a UI |
| Adapt | Narrow `globs` to this repository's UI packages. |

- Icon-only controls need `aria-label`. Use real `<button>` / `<a>` /
  `<NavLink>`, not clickable `div`s.
- Keep skip links and named `<nav>`. Form inputs need visible labels.
- Do not convey state by color alone (include text or `aria-live` for errors).
- Keyboard: new interactive elements must be reachable without a pointer.
- Tester: add at least one `a11y` row in `qa-test-cases.md` when the
  specification has UI.
